  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8230;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be a sample space of raddom experiment such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;for every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Then the number of elements in the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8834;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is _____.",
    "image": null
